{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nEach application domain defines what identifies a node across runs. Changes to a node's contents or outgoing edges preserve its identity.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests against the text of `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types`. The text has two obligations: (1) a domain defines what identifies a node across runs, and (2) changes to a node's contents or outgoing edges preserve its identity. I did not read implementation source.\n\n**Obligation 1: identity across runs.**\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` covers it for the Habeas domain. It checks every `HabeasNode` variant. It asserts each variant's exact path segments. It asserts a freshly reconstructed `HabeasDomain` with a new `OutlineCache` gives an equal path. It asserts every field change (`FixmeId` fields, `SiteReview` requirement, resource scheme, location and selector) gives a distinct path. It also checks that the opaque segments are preserved.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` covers it for an enum-identified domain. It asserts equal paths from a fresh domain and distinct identities for requirement and source nodes. It asserts the exact path segments. It also checks that evidence stored for a requirement node is not returned for the source node.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` covers it for a domain with an opaque node type. It asserts the path `[\"relationships\",\"1\"]` and that different nodes get different paths.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` covers it for a second domain. It stores and loads evidence by node and criterion, and the loaded record's `source_node_id` equals the stored one.\n\n**Obligation 2: identity preserved when contents or edges change.**\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` changes `src/lib.rs`, first adding an `{impl}` reference and then editing the function body. The subject requirement node's outgoing edges go from empty to one source node. That source node's identity is `HabeasNode::from(InputSelector::Outline{...})`, and it is unchanged. After the body edit, the same node data is re-interned in a new domain. Its fingerprint differs, but it resolves to the same node. So the test shows contents and edges change while identity does not.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_shares_discovery_snapshots_with_tracked_reads]` rewrites the file after discovery. The source node's path is still `[\"source\",\"repo\",\"src/lib.rs\",\"fn[helper]\"]`. The edge from the subject to that source node is unchanged.\n\nA domain that put a content hash or edge list into node identity would fail these assertions, so they enforce the requirement. The remaining test items (`default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix`, `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent`) also exercise identity-keyed reads and storage, but I did not rely on them. I found no gap and no marking gap.",
  "references": "78521c46b3d7e947f2b1c262b4ddec789e08bce27062b8e4b6647057a600a11c",
